    "description": "VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT Position: Executive Assistant to the Group CEO Company: Adil Corporate Group (ACG) Duty Station: Addis Ababa, Ethiopia Employment Type: Full-Time Gender : Preferably Female Department: Office of the Group CEO Reports To: Group Chief Executive Officer About Adil Corporate Group Adil Corporate Group (ACG) is a diversified business group engaged in multiple investment and business sectors. The Group is committed to sustainable growth, strategic investment, operational excellence, and the development of competitive business ventures. ACG is seeking a highly competent, proactive, organized, and results-oriented Executive Assistant to the Group CEO to provide high-level executive, administrative, communication, and management coordination support to the Group CEO. 1. Job Purpose The Executive Assistant to the Group CEO is responsible for providing comprehensive executive support and ensuring effective coordination, communication, documentation, and follow-up of the CEO's priorities, directives, decisions, and strategic assignments. In addition, Executive Assistant is responsible for the secretary roles. And work on the documentation of all files related to ACG. The position serves as a central coordination point between the Group CEO, Deputy Group CEO, subsidiary Managing Directors/General Managers, department heads, and external stakeholders. Beyond conventional administrative support, the role is expected to strengthen the effectiveness of the CEO's Office by tracking management commitments, monitoring the implementation of executive decisions, ensuring timely submission of reports, identifying pending assignments, and escalating critical matters requiring the CEO's attention. 2. Key Duties and Responsibilities A. Executive and Administrative Support Manage and organize the Group CEO's daily schedule, appointments, meetings, and official engagements. Prioritize incoming communications, requests, correspondence, and executive assignments. Prepare executive briefs, presentations, reports, letters, memoranda, and other official documents. Coordinate domestic and international travel arrangements and official engagements. Maintain an efficient filing and documentation system for the CEO's Office. Anticipate the CEO's administrative and coordination needs and provide proactive support. B. CEO Directives and Management Decision Follow-Up Maintain a centralized CEO Directives and Action Tracking Register. Record CEO instructions, management decisions, assignments, responsible persons, deadlines, and implementation status. Follow up with responsible executives, department heads, and subsidiary management to ensure timely implementation. Prepare regular updates highlighting completed, ongoing, delayed, and outstanding assignments. Identify overdue actions, implementation gaps, and unresolved management issues and escalate them to the CEO. Ensure that decisions made during executive meetings are translated into clear action points with assigned responsibilities and deadlines. Follow up on priority projects and strategic initiatives as directed by the CEO. C. Executive Coordination and Organizational Communication Serve as the primary coordination link between the Group CEO, Deputy Group CEO, subsidiary General Managers, and department heads. Facilitate timely communication and information exchange across the Group. Coordinate the submission of periodic performance reports, departmental updates, and subsidiary reports. Follow up on reporting deadlines and communicate delays to the responsible executives. Ensure that important organizational issues and developments are promptly brought to the CEO's attention. Coordinate special assignments and management instructions issued by the CEO. D. Executive Meetings and Management Review Organize and coordinate Group Executive Committee meetings, management review meetings, board meetings, and other executive engagements. Prepare meeting agendas, background documents, presentations, and briefing materials. Record accurate minutes of meetings, decisions, resolutions, and action points. Maintain a meeting resolution and decision-tracking register. Follow up on the implementation of meeting resolutions and agreed management actions. Prepare consolidated follow-up reports for the CEO. E. Executive Reporting and Management Information Collect, organize, and consolidate reports from subsidiaries and Group departments. Prepare concise executive summaries highlighting key performance developments, major achievements, challenges, risks, and pending decisions. Support the CEO in reviewing organizational performance and management updates. Maintain a systematic record of important management decisions, commitments, correspondence, and executive assignments. Ensure that the CEO receives accurate, relevant, and timely information for effective decision-making. Highlight critical financial, operational, legal, reputational, and organizational matters requiring management attention. F. Stakeholder and Official Communication Draft and manage professional correspondence, emails, letters, and official communications on behalf of the CEO. Coordinate communications with government institutions, investors, business partners, clients, and other stakeholders as assigned. Facilitate the preparation and coordination of official meetings and engagements. Handle confidential and sensitive communications with professionalism and discretion. Represent the CEO's Office in routine coordination matters when formally authorized. G. Special Assignments and Strategic Support Coordinate special projects, assignments, and strategic initiatives delegated by the CEO. Conduct preliminary information gathering and research to support executive decisions. Assist in preparing management presentations, strategic briefs, and business reports. Follow up on critical organizational priorities and cross-functional assignments. Provide administrative and coordination support for investment, partnership, and business development engagements as required. H. Executive Office and Administrative Support Manage the CEO’s daily schedule and appointments. Arrange meetings, conferences, and official engagements. Receive visitors and coordinate appointments with the CEO. Prepare correspondence, letters, memos, and official communications. Maintain and organize confidential executive documents and records. Handle incoming and outgoing",
