    "description": "About the Job The Treasury and Tax Lead is responsible for managing the company’s treasury operations, cash flow, liquidity, banking relationships, tax compliance, and tax-related risk. The position ensures the availability and efficient utilization of funds, timely settlement of financial obligations, compliance with applicable tax laws and regulations, and effective management of treasury and tax activities in support of EAND’s operational and financial objectives. Key Responsibilities A. Treasury and Cash Management Prepare and monitor daily, weekly, and monthly cash flow forecasts to ensure adequate liquidity for operational and financial obligations. Monitor cash balances, bank accounts, collections, payments, and fund utilization to ensure effective cash management. Coordinate the timely settlement of suppliers, employees, statutory obligations, loan repayments, and other approved financial commitments. Optimize cash utilization and minimize idle funds, financing costs, and liquidity risks. Monitor cash flow requirements arising from cement distribution, raw material and supply operations, and other business activities. Ensure proper planning and management of cash shortages, surpluses, and funding requirements. B. Banking and Financial Facilities Management Manage operational relationships with banks and other financial institutions. Coordinate bank transfers, payments, account reconciliations, bank confirmations, and other treasury transactions. Monitor bank loans, overdrafts, credit facilities, guarantees, letters of credit, and other financial instruments, as applicable. Follow up on facility utilization, repayment schedules, interest charges, fees, and financing terms. Coordinate the preparation of banking documents and requests for new or renewed financial facilities. Identify opportunities to improve banking services, transaction efficiency, and financing costs. C. Treasury Controls and Risk Management Ensure treasury transactions are conducted in accordance with approved financial policies, procedures, authorization limits, and internal control requirements. Maintain proper segregation of duties between payment initiation, approval, execution, and reconciliation. Monitor treasury-related financial risks, including liquidity, banking, interest rate, foreign exchange, and payment risks, where applicable. Ensure accurate and timely bank reconciliation and investigate outstanding or unusual transactions. Maintain proper treasury records, supporting documents, and audit trails. Identify control weaknesses and recommend corrective measures to strengthen treasury operations. D. Tax Compliance and Administration Ensure timely preparation, declaration, and settlement of applicable taxes in accordance with Ethiopian tax laws, regulations, and directives. Coordinate the preparation and submission of VAT, withholding tax, income tax, payroll-related taxes, and other applicable statutory tax declarations. Review tax computations, supporting schedules, reconciliations, and payment obligations to ensure accuracy and compliance. Ensure proper tax treatment of business transactions, supplier payments, customer transactions, imports, and other applicable financial activities. Monitor changes in tax laws, regulations, directives, and administrative practices and assess their implications for EAND. Maintain proper tax records, supporting documents, and statutory registers for compliance and audit purposes. E. Tax Planning, Advisory and Risk Management Provide tax-related advice to management and relevant departments on business transactions, contracts, procurement, sales, and operational decisions. Identify tax exposures, compliance risks, potential penalties, and opportunities for legitimate tax optimization. Review business transactions and financial arrangements to ensure appropriate tax treatment and documentation. Coordinate tax audits, tax assessments, investigations, and correspondence with tax authorities. Follow up on tax audit findings, assessments, disputed tax liabilities, refunds, credits, and outstanding tax matters. Recommend appropriate tax risk mitigation measures and improvements to tax processes and controls. F. Reporting, Coordination and Continuous Improvement Prepare periodic treasury, cash flow, banking, tax compliance, and financial risk reports for management. Provide timely information on cash position, funding requirements, tax liabilities, payment commitments, and treasury performance. Coordinate with Accounting, Finance, Sales, Procurement, HR, Operations, and other departments to ensure accurate financial information and compliance. Support budget preparation, financial planning, forecasting, and working capital management. Participate in internal and external audits and provide required information and documentation. Ensure effective utilization of ERP and other financial systems for treasury, banking, payment, and tax processes. Recommend and implement improvements to treasury and tax procedures, reporting, automation, and operational efficiency.",
