    "description": "Background ABH Partners Plc is a leading multidisciplinary consultancy and human resource management firm with extensive expertise in delivering strategic organizational solutions across diverse sectors. Operating with a strong commitment to excellence, compliance, and operational efficiency, ABH Partners supports major national and international enterprises in scaling their operations through end-to-end talent acquisition, workforce administration, and performance management services. In its capacity as an authorized Super Agent for Safaricom, ABH Partners Plc is mandated to source, recruit, and onboard high-caliber, competitive talent to drive Safaricom’s commercial and operational expansion. Beyond recruitment, ABH Partners assumes comprehensive responsibility for payroll administration, statutory compliance, contract management, and continuous employment performance oversight—ensuring that deployed teams are fully equipped, motivated, and aligned with Safaricom’s rigorous service and distribution standards. Job Description Position: Trade Acquisition & Distribution Representative (TADR) Required No .:15 Reports to: Safaricom Regional Sales Manager and Regional Acquisition Manager Location: Addis Ababa Employment type: Contract Key Responsibilities Acquisition Achieve daily, weekly, and monthly sales targets by driving quality gross additions for individual customers. Prospect, onboard, and activate small and medium businesses on Safaricom products and services. Conduct training for acquisition agents on eKYC processes to ensure compliance and efficiency. Deliver consumer and merchant training to create awareness and promote Safaricom products and services. Ensure branding, merchandising, and compliance standards are consistently maintained across all channels. Deploy BTL marketing materials in all outlets according to merchandising guidelines. Prepare and submit reports on trade performance,training coverage, market insights, competitor activities, float levels, and product availability. 2. Distribution Meet daily, weekly, and monthly sales and distribution targets. Conduct regular sales visits to retailers to understand their needs, address challenges, and build strong relationships. Make sure products and float are always available for retailers and consumers. Support distributors and retailer outlets in achieving sales targets through in-market promotions and visibility programs. Coach and train distributor staff and merchants on customer relationship management, new or update product knowledge, and service delivery. Maintain branding, merchandising, and compliance standards across all touchpoints. Ensure deployment of BTL materials in line with merchandising standards. Provide regular reports on trade performance,training activities, market intelligence, and product / float availability. Perform any additional tasks assigned by the immediate supervisor. 3.M-Pesa Meet daily, weekly, and monthly sales targets on new Agents, float and visibility Identify and prospect new merchants, focusing on activation and visibility placement. Execute market activation initiatives through regular visits and training sessions for merchants. Facilitate the onboarding of new merchants, ensuring they understand product offerings and operational processes. Distribution and territory management by ensuring that all M‐PESA agents’ outlets are visited as per assigned route plan. Ensure float availability for agents to support merchant transactions. Utilize working tools and reporting systems to track performance and manage day-to-day operations effectively. Consumer training and awareness of Safaricom products and services. Ensuring branding and compliance standards are maintained across all channels. Ensuring all BTL materials are deployed to all outlets as per merchandising standards. Report on trade performance, training coverage, market activities, market intelligence, and float and product availability in the market amongst other . Work on every additional work given by the immediate supervisor.",
