    "description": "Background Christoffel Blindenmission (CBM ) is an international Christian development organisation. CBM envisages an inclusive world in which all people enjoy their human rights and achieve their full potential. CBM’s aim is to contribute to transformative change in structures, systems and attitudes which will bring about an improved quality of life for people with disabilities living in poverty, their families and their communities. Based on its Christian values and over 100 years of professional expertise, CBM addresses poverty as a cause, and a consequence, of disability, and works in partnership to create a society for all. CBM provides technical and financial support to partners and works with them to achieve the quality of lives improvement of persons with disabilities in Ethiopia. CBM Ethiopia Country Office (CO) as a development partner of Ethiopia, in partnership with key stakeholders, is engaged in growth, development and transformation processes of the country in the areas of Health, Education, Livelihoods, Emergency and Food security, Social and Empowerment of persons with disabilities, their families and those who are at risk of disability, since 1967 G.C. Since then, the quality of lives of hundreds of thousands of people has been improved by working in partnership with and through government partners, development partners, local and international NGOs, International humanitarian and professional clubs, organizations of persons with disabilities (OPDs), civil society organizations (CSOs), church-based institutions and communities. In order to improve the quality of lives of persons with disabilities and those at risk of disability, CBM has been focusing on capacity development of partners, disability and inclusive development, program and organizational sustainability; networking and alliance building. Moreover, CBM, through its long-lasting experience (50 years) in developing and strengthening partnerships, has contributed to technically and financially supporting its partners, in order to holistically empower persons with disabilities and their families as well as those at risk of disability, to lead a fulfilling and dignified life in an inclusive society. The management of CBM Ethiopia Country Office seeks the services of an Audit Firm to conduct a Statutory Audit The CBM Ethiopia CO Program and Administration budget for the year 2026 is ETB 160,000,000.00. There are 25 annual finance transaction box files.",
